From ac082e360b78f1dee58b1d97f2e9d4eb44d4e807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:25:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(scratchpad): fade a closing member above the pad
 backdrop

A window closed inside a scratchpad left its close snapshot under the pad's
own dim rect and blur. The pad then attenuated the snapshot instead of letting
it fade: a mid-fade sample read 18 where a plain floating window reads 90, and
hiding the pad mid-close left the snapshot on screen after the pad was gone.

Capture a member's snapshot into a per-snapshot layer of the pad tree, on the
member's pad output and clipped to it, and drive the snapshot's opacity with
that pad's backdrop fade so a hide takes a mid-fade snapshot with it. The
layer is dropped when the server reaps the snapshot, which is also how an
output release reaps it.

tests/harness/checks/animation/scratchpad_close.sh pins both halves: the
member's mid-fade sample matches the floating control, and a pad hidden
mid-close leaves nothing on screen (112 before the multiplier).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
