From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:12:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(scratchpad): keep the pad's fade bookkeeping honest
 across reloads

External review follow-ups.

An owner's fade is applied per node even when a lifecycle shader composites the snapshot as one image: the shader
API has no group-opacity uniform, so a pad hide attenuates each contribution inside the composite. Say so where the
composited branch is chosen instead of implying the nodes stay opaque.

`animatesOn()` now answers for a tracked snapshot too, so the manager keeps the per-output animation invariant.
`applyConfig()` pushes its snapped fades to tracked snapshots instead of waiting for a tick, and
`refreshOutputGeometry()` re-clips a mid-fade wrapper to its output's new box.

The pin grows a hot-unplug leg: destroy the output the pad is actually on, mid-fade, then `settle`. It fails with
"an animation is running on the frozen animation clock" when the output-removal reap forgets the wrapper.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
